.TH RFILE 1 "October 2026" "rfile 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfile \- identify files using a bounded Rust magic engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfile
.RI [ options ] " FILE..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
rfile independently evaluates file magic rules and built-in text and format
recognizers. It embeds rules from file 5.48, commit
41b1123083ab0bbdfe32f6d4ec14f6aec9a91e59.
A FILE of - reads standard input. No operands prints usage and exits with status 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -b , " --brief"
Omit filenames.
.TP
.BR -i , " --mime"
Print MIME type and encoding. --mime-type and --mime-encoding select either half.
.TP
.BR -k , " --keep-going"
Continue after matches. Normal output escapes embedded newlines as octal bytes.
.TP
.BI "-m " PATHS
Load source rules or v21 compiled databases. Unix lists are colon-separated.
.TP
.BI "-f " LIST
Read LF-separated filenames immediately using options selected so far.
A LIST of - reads filenames from standard input.
.TP
.BR -L , " -h"
Follow or do not follow symbolic links. POSIXLY_CORRECT selects following by default.
.TP
.BR -z , " -Z"
Inspect one gzip/zlib layer. -Z hides the outer description.
Other codecs return an explicit unsupported error when decompression is requested.
.TP
.BR -r , " -0 , " -N , " -n"
Print raw bytes; add NUL after filename; omit padding; flush each record.
Repeating -0 also NUL-terminates the result and removes the separator.
.TP
.BI "-F " SEP
Use SEP instead of the filename colon.
.TP
.BR -E , " -s , " -p"
Report filesystem failures as errors; permit device reads; restore access times.
.TP
.BI "-e " TEST
Exclude a detector. See --help for names. --exclude-quiet ignores unknown names.
.TP
.BI "-P " NAME=VALUE
Set a resource parameter. Additional Rust budgets are steps, work and output.
.TP
.BR --extension , " --apple"
Print extension or Apple annotations.
.TP
.BR -C , " -c , " -l"
Compile, check or list rules. Use -m to select the source/database.
Check/list/debug diagnostic text differs from C file.
.TP
.BR -S , " -v , " --help"
Accept sandbox-disable option; display version/features; display help.
This build has no kernel sandbox.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
MAGIC supplies a database list when -m is absent. HOME supplies optional .magic
configuration before the embedded default. POSIXLY_CORRECT enables symlink following.
Filename escaping and display alignment currently implement the C locale profile.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means classification completed, including unknown data and ordinary per-file
filesystem diagnostics. -E, setup failures, resource errors and failed writes
produce status 1. A classification is a heuristic, not validation of the whole file.
.SH FILES
The default rules are embedded; normal operation needs neither libmagic nor a C
compiler. See data/UPSTREAM.json and data/SOURCES.json for data provenance.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Version 0.1.0 is tested on x86_64 Linux. Full CDF summaries, some ELF/core details,
local-time formatting, POSIX backreferences/collation, other decompression codecs,
and kernel sandboxing remain incomplete. See docs/06-implementation-status.md
for compatibility results and release gates. No C ABI is provided.
